<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Baesweiler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1371">1371</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Baesweiler was fought on 22 August 1371 near Baesweiler, north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a>, between Duke Wenceslaus of Brabant and Duke William II of Jülich, allied with Edward of Guelders. Wenceslaus's army was defeated and he was captured, though Edward of Guelders was mortally wounded. The duke had to pay a heavy ransom, and the defeat weakened Brabant's standing in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-baesweiler.jpg" alt="Battle of Baesweiler" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Hinderikus Egenberger (schilder) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anno_1371._Hertog_Eduard_van_Gelre_wordt_te_Baesweiler_verraderlijk_doodgeschoten,_objectnr_SA_4889.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
